      "updated": 1756795521449,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n# Create helpful scripts for network troubleshooting\ncat > /home/ec2-user/network-check.sh << 'NETCHECK'\n#!/bin/bash\necho \"=== Network Troubleshooting Script ===\"\necho \"Date: $(date)\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Network Interfaces ===\"\nip addr show\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Routing Table ===\"\nip route show\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== DNS Configuration ===\"\ncat /etc/resolv.conf\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Listening Ports ===\"\nss -tlnp\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Established Connections ===\"\nss -o state established\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Firewall Rules (iptables) ===\"\nsudo iptables -L -n\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Process List ===\"\nps aux | head -20\nNETCHECK\n\nchmod +x /home/ec2-user/network-check.sh\nchown ec2-user:ec2-user /home/ec2-user/network-check.sh\n\n# Create SSH connection helper script\ncat > /home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh << 'SSHHELPER'\n#!/bin/bash\nPRIVATE_IP=\"$${1:-10.0.253.166}\"\n\necho \"Connecting to private instance at $$PRIVATE_IP\"\necho \"Testing connectivity first...\"\n\n# Test SSH port\nif nc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 22 2>/dev/null; then\n    echo \"✅ SSH port 22 is reachable\"\nelse\n    echo \"❌ SSH port 22 is NOT reachable\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\n# Test web service port\nif nc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 8080 2>/dev/null; then\n    echo \"✅ Web service port 8080 is reachable\"\nelse\n    echo \"❌ Web service port 8080 is NOT reachable\"\nfi\n\necho \"Attempting SSH connection...\"\nssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no ubuntu@$$PRIVATE_IP\nSSHHELPER\n\nchmod +x /home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh\nchown ec2-user:ec2-user /home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh\n\n# Create port testing script\ncat > /home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh << 'PORTTEST'\n#!/bin/bash\nPRIVATE_IP=\"$${1:-10.0.253.166}\"\n\necho \"=== Port Connectivity Test to $$PRIVATE_IP ===\"\necho \"Date: $$(date)\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing SSH (port 22):\"\nnc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 22\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing HTTP (port 80):\"\nnc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 80\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing Web Service (port 8080):\"\nnc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 8080\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing HTTP response from web service:\"\ncurl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://$$PRIVATE_IP:8080 || echo \"Failed to connect to web service\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing Nginx response:\"\ncurl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://$$PRIVATE_IP:80 || echo \"Failed to connect to Nginx\"\nPORTTEST\n\nchmod +x /home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh\nchown ec2-user:ec2-user /home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh\n\n# Create daily log rotation for troubleshooting\ncat > /etc/logrotate.d/user-troubleshooting << 'LOGROTATE'\n/var/log/user-data.log {\n    daily\n    rotate 7\n    compress\n    missingok\n    notifempty\n    create 0644 root root\n}\nLOGROTATE\n\n# Set up useful aliases for ec2-user\ncat >> /home/ec2-user/.bashrc << 'ALIASES'\n\n# Network troubleshooting aliases\nalias netcheck='/home/ec2-user/network-check.sh'\nalias testports='/home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh'\nalias connectprivate='/home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh'\nalias ports='ss -tlnp'\nalias connections='ss -o state established'\nalias listening='ss -tlnp | grep LISTEN'\n\n# Helpful shortcuts\nalias ll='ls -la'\nalias la='ls -A'\nalias l='ls -CF'\nALIASES\n\n# Create a welcome message\ncat > /etc/motd << 'MOTD'\n========================================\n🏰 SSH Bastion Host - Network Toolkit\n========================================\n\nAvailable network troubleshooting tools:\n• netcheck          - Complete network status\n• testports [IP]     - Test connectivity to private instance\n• connectprivate [IP]- Connect to private instance\n• ports             - Show listening ports\n• connections       - Show established connections\n• listening         - Show only listening services\n\nInstalled tools:\n• ss, netstat       - Network connections\n• lsof              - Open files/ports\n• tcpdump           - Packet capture\n• nmap              - Network scanning\n• telnet, nc        - Connection testing\n• curl, wget        - HTTP clients\n\nLog files:\n• /var/log/user-data.log - Setup script log\n• /var/log/messages      - System messages\n\n========================================\nMOTD\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n# Create helpful scripts for network troubleshooting\ncat > /home/ec2-user/network-check.sh << 'NETCHECK'\n#!/bin/bash\necho \"=== Network Troubleshooting Script ===\"\necho \"Date: $(date)\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Network Interfaces ===\"\nip addr show\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Routing Table ===\"\nip route show\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== DNS Configuration ===\"\ncat /etc/resolv.conf\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Listening Ports ===\"\nss -tlnp\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Established Connections ===\"\nss -o state established\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Firewall Rules (iptables) ===\"\nsudo iptables -L -n\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== Process List ===\"\nps aux | head -20\nNETCHECK\n\nchmod +x /home/ec2-user/network-check.sh\nchown ec2-user:ec2-user /home/ec2-user/network-check.sh\n\n# Create SSH connection helper script\ncat > /home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh << 'SSHHELPER'\n#!/bin/bash\nPRIVATE_IP=\"$${1:-10.0.253.166}\"\n\necho \"Connecting to private instance at $$PRIVATE_IP\"\necho \"Testing connectivity first...\"\n\n# Test SSH port\nif nc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 22 2>/dev/null; then\n    echo \"✅ SSH port 22 is reachable\"\nelse\n    echo \"❌ SSH port 22 is NOT reachable\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\n# Test web service port\nif nc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 8080 2>/dev/null; then\n    echo \"✅ Web service port 8080 is reachable\"\nelse\n    echo \"❌ Web service port 8080 is NOT reachable\"\nfi\n\necho \"Attempting SSH connection...\"\nssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no ubuntu@$$PRIVATE_IP\nSSHHELPER\n\nchmod +x /home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh\nchown ec2-user:ec2-user /home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh\n\n# Create port testing script\ncat > /home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh << 'PORTTEST'\n#!/bin/bash\nPRIVATE_IP=\"$${1:-10.0.253.166}\"\n\necho \"=== Port Connectivity Test to $$PRIVATE_IP ===\"\necho \"Date: $$(date)\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing SSH (port 22):\"\nnc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 22\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing HTTP (port 80):\"\nnc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 80\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing Web Service (port 8080):\"\nnc -zv $$PRIVATE_IP 8080\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing HTTP response from web service:\"\ncurl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://$$PRIVATE_IP:8080 || echo \"Failed to connect to web service\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"Testing Nginx response:\"\ncurl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://$$PRIVATE_IP:80 || echo \"Failed to connect to Nginx\"\nPORTTEST\n\nchmod +x /home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh\nchown ec2-user:ec2-user /home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh\n\n# Create daily log rotation for troubleshooting\ncat > /etc/logrotate.d/user-troubleshooting << 'LOGROTATE'\n/var/log/user-data.log {\n    daily\n    rotate 7\n    compress\n    missingok\n    notifempty\n    create 0644 root root\n}\nLOGROTATE\n\n# Set up useful aliases for ec2-user\ncat >> /home/ec2-user/.bashrc << 'ALIASES'\n\n# Network troubleshooting aliases\nalias netcheck='/home/ec2-user/network-check.sh'\nalias testports='/home/ec2-user/test-ports.sh'\nalias connectprivate='/home/ec2-user/connect-to-private.sh'\nalias ports='ss -tlnp'\nalias connections='ss -o state established'\nalias listening='ss -tlnp | grep LISTEN'\n\n# Helpful shortcuts\nalias ll='ls -la'\nalias la='ls -A'\nalias l='ls -CF'\nALIASES\n\n# Create a welcome message\ncat > /etc/motd << 'MOTD'\n========================================\n🏰 SSH Bastion Host - Network Toolkit\n========================================\n\nAvailable network troubleshooting tools:\n• netcheck          - Complete network status\n• testports [IP]     - Test connectivity to private instance\n• connectprivate [IP]- Connect to private instance\n• ports             - Show listening ports\n• connections       - Show established connections\n• listening         - Show only listening services\n\nInstalled tools:\n• ss, netstat       - Network connections\n• lsof              - Open files/ports\n• tcpdump           - Packet capture\n• nmap              - Network scanning\n• telnet, nc        - Connection testing\n• curl, wget        - HTTP clients\n\nLog files:\n• /var/log/user-data.log - Setup script log\n• /var/log/messages      - System messages\n\n========================================\nMOTD\n",
