      "versionNonce": 1642740000,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1756796309863,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Verify `ssh-agent` process is running on your laptop, you'll see a line with its proceess ID and description\n# another method to check if `ssh-agent` is running, you can check environment variable `echo $SSH_AUTH_SOCK`\n$ ps -e | grep [s]sh-agent\n33399 ??         0:00.24 /usr/bin/ssh-agent -l\n\n# Verify \n$ ssh-add -l\nThe agent has no identities.\n\n# To remove identities\n$ ssh-add -D\nAll identities removed.\n\n# Connect from your laptop to bastion-host\nssh -i ssh-privatekey.pem ec2-user@3.1.38.210\n\n# option 1\n$ ss -an 2>/dev/null | grep :22\ntcp   LISTEN 0      128                                0.0.0.0:22               0.0.0.0:*           \ntcp   ESTAB  0      36                              10.0.1.252:22           121.6.81.90:52808       \ntcp   LISTEN 0      128                                   [::]:22                  [::]:*       \n\n# option 2\n$ sudo lsof -i :22\nCOMMAND   PID     USER   FD   TYPE DEVICE SIZE/OFF NODE NAME\nsshd     3113     root    3u  IPv4  18692      0t0  TCP *:ssh (LISTEN)\nsshd     3113     root    4u  IPv6  18701      0t0  TCP *:ssh (LISTEN)\nsshd    32454     root    3u  IPv4  51383      0t0  TCP ip-10-0-1-252.ap-southeast-1.compute.internal:ssh->bb121-6-81-90.singnet.com.sg:52808 (ESTABLISHED)\nsshd    32489 ec2-user    3u  IPv4  51383      0t0  TCP ip-10-0-1-252.ap-southeast-1.compute.internal:ssh->bb121-6-81-90.singnet.com.sg:52808 (ESTABLISHED)\n\n# option 2\n$ netstat -an | grep ESTABLISHED\ntcp        0     36 10.0.1.252:22           121.6.81.90:52808       ESTABLISHED",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Verify `ssh-agent` process is running on your laptop, you'll see a line with its proceess ID and description\n# another method to check if `ssh-agent` is running, you can check environment variable `echo $SSH_AUTH_SOCK`\n$ ps -e | grep [s]sh-agent\n33399 ??         0:00.24 /usr/bin/ssh-agent -l\n\n# Verify \n$ ssh-add -l\nThe agent has no identities.\n\n# To remove identities\n$ ssh-add -D\nAll identities removed.\n\n# Connect from your laptop to bastion-host\nssh -i ssh-privatekey.pem ec2-user@3.1.38.210\n\n# option 1\n$ ss -an 2>/dev/null | grep :22\ntcp   LISTEN 0      128                                0.0.0.0:22               0.0.0.0:*           \ntcp   ESTAB  0      36                              10.0.1.252:22           121.6.81.90:52808       \ntcp   LISTEN 0      128                                   [::]:22                  [::]:*       \n\n# option 2\n$ sudo lsof -i :22\nCOMMAND   PID     USER   FD   TYPE DEVICE SIZE/OFF NODE NAME\nsshd     3113     root    3u  IPv4  18692      0t0  TCP *:ssh (LISTEN)\nsshd     3113     root    4u  IPv6  18701      0t0  TCP *:ssh (LISTEN)\nsshd    32454     root    3u  IPv4  51383      0t0  TCP ip-10-0-1-252.ap-southeast-1.compute.internal:ssh->bb121-6-81-90.singnet.com.sg:52808 (ESTABLISHED)\nsshd    32489 ec2-user    3u  IPv4  51383      0t0  TCP ip-10-0-1-252.ap-southeast-1.compute.internal:ssh->bb121-6-81-90.singnet.com.sg:52808 (ESTABLISHED)\n\n# option 2\n$ netstat -an | grep ESTABLISHED\ntcp        0     36 10.0.1.252:22           121.6.81.90:52808       ESTABLISHED",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
