    {
      "id": "b7jG67OK0D_k-X2v-MAIx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -10001.724506829654,
      "y": 8844.789890752472,
      "width": 3326.39794921875,
      "height": 840,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bPv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 172262639,
      "version": 363,
      "versionNonce": 1148013845,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1759035118656,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Note:\n1 - You executed `aws ssm start-session --target i-09bf42304e14bf70f`, which launched the plug-in `session-manager-plugin` to manage the connection.\n \n\n2 - JSON Payload (Session Configuration)\nThe plugin receives a JSON object with session details from AWS SSM:\n\n* SessionId: Unique identifier for this session (sai.linnthu@hashicorp.com-tqqn6leoezy8g66gihdd3r3de8).\n\n* TokenValue: A temporary, encrypted token used to authenticate your session with AWS. This ensures only authorized users can connect.\n\n* StreamUrl: The WebSocket URL (wss://ssmmessages.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/...) used for real-time data streaming between your local machine and the instance. This is how commands/output are transmitted securely.\n\n* ResponseMetadata: Metadata from the AWS API call that started the session, including:\n        * RequestId: AWS internal ID for the session request.\n        * HTTPStatusCode: 200 (success).\n        * HTTPHeaders: Technical details about the API response.\n\n* ap-southeast-1: The AWS region where the session was initiated.\n* StartSession: The SSM API operation used.\n* {\"Target\": \"i-09bf42304e14bf70f\"}: The target EC2 instance ID.\n* https://ssm.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com: The SSM service endpoint.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Note:\n1 - You executed `aws ssm start-session --target i-09bf42304e14bf70f`, which launched the plug-in `session-manager-plugin` to manage the connection.\n \n\n2 - JSON Payload (Session Configuration)\nThe plugin receives a JSON object with session details from AWS SSM:\n\n* SessionId: Unique identifier for this session (sai.linnthu@hashicorp.com-tqqn6leoezy8g66gihdd3r3de8).\n\n* TokenValue: A temporary, encrypted token used to authenticate your session with AWS. This ensures only authorized users can connect.\n\n* StreamUrl: The WebSocket URL (wss://ssmmessages.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/...) used for real-time data streaming between your local machine and the instance. This is how commands/output are transmitted securely.\n\n* ResponseMetadata: Metadata from the AWS API call that started the session, including:\n        * RequestId: AWS internal ID for the session request.\n        * HTTPStatusCode: 200 (success).\n        * HTTPHeaders: Technical details about the API response.\n\n* ap-southeast-1: The AWS region where the session was initiated.\n* StartSession: The SSM API operation used.\n* {\"Target\": \"i-09bf42304e14bf70f\"}: The target EC2 instance ID.\n* https://ssm.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com: The SSM service endpoint.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
