    {
      "id": "fTShHcLwGgayoBkg7x6_2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8766.012997529273,
      "y": 10154.179794752039,
      "width": 3097.115234375,
      "height": 640.0044821382077,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1775068655,
      "version": 246,
      "versionNonce": 551831905,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1757423904266,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. You run aws ssm start-session --target i-09bf42304e14bf70f.\n\n2. The AWS CLI calls the SSM API, which returns session details (token, WebSocket URL).\n\n3. The session-manager-plugin uses these details to establish a secure WebSocket connection to AWS.\n\n4. AWS relays data between your local computer's shell and the SSM agent on the EC2 instance.\n\n5. You get an interactive shell session without needing SSH keys or open ports.",
      "fontSize": 56.88928730117401,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. You run aws ssm start-session --target i-09bf42304e14bf70f.\n\n2. The AWS CLI calls the SSM API, which returns session details (token, WebSocket URL).\n\n3. The session-manager-plugin uses these details to establish a secure WebSocket connection to AWS.\n\n4. AWS relays data between your local computer's shell and the SSM agent on the EC2 instance.\n\n5. You get an interactive shell session without needing SSH keys or open ports.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
